<p>A herniated disc occurs when pressure from the surrounding vertebrae forces the soft center through the outer layer. The displaced material can press on nearby nerves, causing pain in the neck or back, or symptoms that travel into the arms or legs.</p>
<h3>What causes herniated discs?</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Aging.</strong> Normal wear and tear breaks down the discs and makes them more prone to injury.</li>
